{#
  T-3.03 — the announcement marquee.

  NOT A REGISTERED HOME SECTION, and the backlog's "New sections: registered in
  twilight.json" is the one line of it not followed. A registered `home.*`
  component renders inside `<main>`, below the header. **The artboard puts this
  bar above the header**, so registering it would place it in the wrong half of
  the page in exchange for an ordering control that would only ever have one
  correct answer. It is theme settings instead — which is also what B6's ruling
  literally says: "announcement text is a theme setting". Recorded in
  /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  ONE STRING, NOT A LIST. The artboard shows two phrases — «كود خصم للتحويل
  البنكي AM5» and «من لحظة الطلب… إلى بابك دون انتظار.» — separated by space. The
  backlog specifies `announcement_text`, singular, so that is what this is: a
  merchant writes both phrases with a separator between them. A collection would
  have been a field the plan does not call for.

  READ ONCE, SCROLLED TWICE. A seamless marquee needs its content duplicated —
  the copy is what fills the gap the first one leaves as it exits. The duplicate
  is `aria-hidden`, so a screen reader reads the announcement exactly once, which
  is the acceptance criterion about repetition.

  It is not a live region and must not become one. The text does not change; it
  merely moves. Announcing it on a timer would interrupt whatever the user was
  reading, repeatedly, for no new information.
#}
{% set announcement_text = theme.settings.get('announcement_text') %}

{% if theme.settings.get('announcement_enabled', true) and announcement_text %}
    <div class="announcement-bar card">
        <div class="announcement-bar__track">
            <span class="announcement-bar__text">{{ announcement_text }}</span>
            <span class="announcement-bar__text" aria-hidden="true">{{ announcement_text }}</span>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
